---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
import { smsBase } from '../../lib/text-cta';

// Every sms link carries the +1 number and a prefill (S339, the sitewide sms rule).
const sms = smsBase + encodeURIComponent('Hi Preston, a question about Gauge and my data: ');

const lastUpdated = '2026-11-18';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Gauge privacy', path: '/gauge/privacy' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Gauge Privacy Policy · Winters Code"
  description="What the Gauge weather app keeps on your phone, what it sends to the National Weather Service and OpenStreetMap, and how it uses your location."
  canonicalPath="/gauge/privacy"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema(crumbs))} />
  </Fragment>

  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-eyebrow mono">GAUGE · PRIVACY POLICY</div>
    <h1 class="h1 legal-h1">Gauge privacy, in plain English.</h1>
    <p class="legal-tagline">
      Gauge is a weather app. It needs a place to show you a forecast, and that is about all
      it needs. Here is exactly what it does with your data.
    </p>
    <p class="small legal-updated">Effective and last updated: {lastUpdated}. Describes Gauge version 0.1.</p>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <p class="legal-lead">
        Short version: no account, no ads, no analytics, no tracking. Gauge has no server of
        its own and sends nothing to me. It talks to two public services, listed below, and
        no others.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Who this covers</h2>
      <p>
        Gauge is made by Winters Code, which is me, Preston Winters, in Bandon, Oregon. This
        policy covers the Gauge app on iPhone and Android.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">What stays on your phone</h2>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>Your saved places, up to 20, and the place you last selected.</li>
        <li>
          A saved copy of recent National Weather Service responses, so Gauge can show a
          forecast with its real age when you are offline.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Gauge makes no backup of its own. On Android, app backup is turned off. On iPhone and
        iPad, your device's own backup may include this data. Uninstalling the app removes it
        from the phone.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">What leaves your phone</h2>
      <p>Gauge talks to two outside services and no others.</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>
          <strong>National Weather Service (api.weather.gov).</strong> To get a forecast and
          alerts, Gauge sends the place's coordinates, rounded to four decimal places (about
          11 meters), in the request address. The requests are: the point lookup
          (<span class="mono">/points</span>) for those coordinates; the active alerts for
          those coordinates; the daily forecast, the hourly forecast and the list of nearby
          observation stations, at the addresses the point lookup returns, all on
          api.weather.gov; and the latest reading from up to the three nearest stations, also
          on api.weather.gov. Requests carry a User-Agent that names Gauge and the Winters
          Code website, as the service asks apps to do.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OpenStreetMap Nominatim (nominatim.openstreetmap.org).</strong> Only when
          you type a US city or ZIP code and submit it, the text you typed is sent to look up
          the place. Nothing else is sent there, and it is never used for your phone's
          location.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Like any internet request, these services can see your phone's internet address. Each
        has its own privacy practices, which I cannot see or change.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Your location</h2>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>Gauge asks for location only when you tap "Use my location", and only while the app is open.</li>
        <li>
          It asks the phone for a low accuracy position. On Android it can ask for approximate
          or precise location, and you can choose approximate.
        </li>
        <li>
          The place is saved on your phone as "Current location", with coordinates rounded to
          four decimal places.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can use Gauge without ever sharing your location, by searching for a US city or
          ZIP code instead.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">What I never do</h2>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>No accounts and no sign-in.</li>
        <li>No ads, and no advertising identifier.</li>
        <li>No analytics, crash-reporting or tracking kits in the app.</li>
        <li>Nothing is sold or shared, because I never receive any of your data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Children</h2>
      <p>Gauge collects no personal information from anyone, including children.</p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">When this changes</h2>
      <p>
        If Gauge changes what it collects, this page changes first, the date at the top moves,
        and the change shows up in the site's public history (<a href="/changelog">/changelog</a>).
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:preston@winterscode.com">preston@winterscode.com</a>, text
        <a href={sms}>541-551-0731</a>, or use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 4px 64px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: 64px 4px 80px;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: 80px 0 96px;
    }
  }

  .legal-eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-copper);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-eyebrow { font-size: 12px; }
  }

  .legal-h1 {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .legal-tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--color-ash-300);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 600px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-tagline { font-size: 19px; }
  }

  .legal-updated {
    margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--color-ash-500);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .legal-body {
    margin-top: 36px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
    color: var(--color-ash-300);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-body { font-size: 16px; }
  }
  .legal-body p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-lead {
    padding: 16px 18px;
    background: rgba(77, 216, 168, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(77, 216, 168, 0.25);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    color: var(--color-ash-100);
    font-style: italic;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 16px !important;
    line-height: 1.6 !important;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-lead {
      font-size: 18px !important;
      padding: 20px 24px;
    }
  }

  .legal-h2 {
    margin-top: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-h2 { margin-top: 28px; }
  }

  .legal-body strong {
    color: var(--color-ash-100);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--color-copper-bright);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--copper-hairline);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  @media (hover: hover) {

    .legal-body a:hover {
    color: var(--color-wc-green);
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-wc-green-dim);
  }}

  .legal-list {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .legal-list li {
    padding-left: 18px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .legal-list li::before {
    content: '·';
    position: absolute;
    left: 4px;
    top: 0;
    color: var(--color-copper);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
